{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789902480,"nonce":"FyTx+CchiW66uEGZAytg5CQQbF4=","title":"Lua: table.move is missing, and unpack, move and sort run off the integers or the array","message":"table.move was not defined (sort.lua 'testing move'). table.unpack(t, i, j) took j through an OptInt whose absent marker is mininteger, so unpack(t, minI, minI) read j as absent, and its loop stepped past j when j was maxinteger, wrapping to minI. A move interrupted by a metamethod's error kept going to the end of a range that could be 2^63 long, and table.sort with a __len of maxinteger tried to copy that many. sort's partition with a comparator that never orders (always true) walked off the array and crashed instead of raising 'invalid order function for sorting', and the error it raises after a comparator has run carried the comparator's line rather than the sort's.","files":null}]}